# API calls stay on the same origin as the app (https://tripmatch.fun/api/...)
# and are proxied server-side to Railway with a 200 rewrite (NOT a redirect),
# so the browser never sees or needs the Railway URL, and query strings
# (e.g. ?sort=latest) pass straight through via :splat.
#
# The trailing "!" forces this rule to win even if something under /api/
# happens to match a static asset path - it must always go to Railway,
# never be served as a local file. This rule MUST stay above the SPA
# fallback below, since Netlify matches rules top-to-bottom.
/api/*  https://travelmatch1.up.railway.app/api/:splat  200!

# SPA fallback for client-side (Angular Router) navigation - must come
# after the API rule above.
/*      /index.html  200
